From 8227c7ba367f87980d758ee6337645d0d073c393 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:17:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/36] ple: a table two threads may read, urgent reads and a
 read-slot reserve (setters, off by default)

The PLE side of STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP (a batch admission's prompt read beside the pipelined slot windows): the
prompt's chunks and the stage-0 windows then gather from the same PleTable at once. Everything here is switched on
by a setter; with the setters off every entry runs the same code in the same order as before.
- PleTable::set_concurrent: the table's own state (the pending token, the prefetch slots) is taken under a lock in
  every public entry (private bodies, so entries that call each other do not lock twice). The rows are read outside
  it: the mapping is read-only, the threaded reader locks itself. bytes_read is atomic, counted once per batch in
  the mapped gather. concurrent_capable(): Mmap mode, or Direct with the I/O worker (not --ple-sync-submit).
- gather_batch(..., urgent) and PleReader::issue(..., urgent): the ticket's reads queue behind the urgent reads
  already waiting and ahead of the rest, also in DirectFile's own queue (submit(..., front); on Linux up to
  max_inflight - 16 submitted reads wait there). Only the read order changes, never a row's bytes.
- PleReader::set_urgent_reserve(n): a non-urgent read is submitted only while more than n of the max_inflight
  slots are free; clamped to max_inflight / 2, 0 without the I/O worker and after close. ReaderStats counts
  urgent tickets and their collect wait; io_report's line is unchanged. PleTable forwards the reserve and the
  counts (io_counts, zeros in Mmap mode).
- Verifier::set_ple_urgent: stage_batch's gather (the batch windows) asks as urgent.
- sycl/: the migrated ple_reader.cpp and direct_file.cpp get the same changes (they build against the shared
  headers, and the shared ngram.cpp calls the new members).
- ple_reader_test --selftest: two threads on one table (6 chunks of 512 tokens against 4-token urgent gathers, Mmap
  and Direct with and without the row cache): every row equal to the format's dequantizer, bytes_read adds up,
  every urgent ticket counted; the single-thread entries under the lock (no self-deadlock); a caller-thread Direct
  table is not concurrent_capable. Read order with inflight 1 and 5 ms injected reads: FIFO without urgent (the
  bulk ticket is done when the later one is), urgent ahead of the bulk; with 64 in flight and a reserve of 16 an
  urgent ticket behind 8000 bulk rows took 3.1 ms, the bulk's tail 336 ms. Reserve clamp, reset on close, none
  without the worker. Both order checks fail with the urgent queueing and the reserve taken out.
- Checked: the selftest passes in build-mmqtab (CMake), in a host-only g++ build, and under ThreadSanitizer
  (host-only g++ -fsanitize=thread, run with `setarch -R`: 0 reports; with bytes_read made non-atomic it reports
  the race), also with the sycl/ copies of ple_reader.cpp and direct_file.cpp linked instead.

